************************************************************************ NewCalls.asm** Copyright (C) 1986-1993 Apple Computer, Inc.* All rights reserved** Original Code* by Dan Oliver************************************************************************* Contains:**	AlertWindow*	CompileText*	ErrorWindow**	GetAuxWindInfo	;added 19-Jan-91 Dave Lyons*	DoModalWindow	;...*	MWGetCtlPart*	MWSetMenuProc*	MWStdDrawProc*	MWSetUpEditMenu*	FindCursorCtl*	ResizeInfoBar	;added 5-Mar-91 DAL*	HandleDiskInsert	;added 12-Mar-91 DAL*********************************************************************************************************************************************** Change History** 22 June 88	Harry Yee** Converted to MAX development system. ** 19 Oct 88	Dan O.** Added internal call compileString.  Made AlertWindow use * compileString call.  TaskMasterContent wasn't being called if * TM_CONTENT was zero.  TaskMasterContent changed to track only* top window.** 11/04/88	Dan O.** Implemented alert string as handle or resource in addition to * already supported pointer.** XX Jan 89	Konstantin** Error window added to Source.** 21-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Fixed returned carry status on ErrorWindow.* Changed hard-coded memory IDs from $1001 to $400E.* Saved a few bytes here and there (all marked).** 14-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Working on AlertWindow.  TS3 will use this version.** (done) Bit 3 of flags = ignore icon width in rectangle computation* (We draw the icon -after- the text now, to support bit 3.)* Doesn't hang if you have a "^" in your alert text.** 10-Dec-90	Dave Lyons** Added check of xxBounds+x2 before PPToPort code, in case we don't* have an icon to draw (discovered by Bill Mitchell/Mensch).** 19-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Adding new call GetAuxWindInfo.** Adding new calls DoModalWindow, MWGetCtlPart, MWSetMenuProc,* MWStdDrawProc, MWSetUpEditMenu, FindCursorCtl.** 22-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Finished adding the modal window calls.** 14-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Bit 31 of the DoModalWindow event hook now translates Apple-period* into Escape for you.** 15-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** DoModalWindow calls SysBeep2(4) if you click in the wrong window.* Removed special handling for zero-length text scraps, since these* no longer cause Line Edit to trash memory.** 17-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** DoModalWindow now calls GetNextEvent with even mask $0FFF, not $FFFF.* We don't fetch any application events.** 28-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** When GetAuxWindInfo expanded its handle, the calculated size was too* low by 4 bytes, so it was trashing 4 bytes of memory.** 3-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed GetAuxWindInfo again; I was really trashing 8 bytes before, and* 4 after the previous fix.  Now it's 0.** 4-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow now has an update routine!** 7-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Make AlertWindow beep when you click outside the window.** 9-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Made ErrorWindow call SysBeep2($CExx) for error numbers $00xx.* Adding alertSoundBit ($0010) to AlertWindow; calls SysBeep2* $C05x, except for icon #1 (custom) and #5 (Disk).** Stop and Note (icons #2 and #4) use sound even if you don't set* the bit asking it to.** 11-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow has key equivalents now.  Default button gets Return,* "Cancel" button gets ESC, Apple-period equals ESC, and all other* buttons get the upper- and lower-case versions of their title's* first letter.  There is no checking for conflicts yet.** 12-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow disk-swap icon gives SysBeep2($C030) instead of $C056* now, if the alertSound bit is on.** 13-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Made ErrorWindow with an error >$FF call SysBeep2($CEFF).* Implemented AlertWindow flag bit $0020, alertSpacingBit.  If you* set this, your up-to-three buttons get allocated from right to* left, in lower-right, left-of-lower-right, and way-left order.** If any button has the same first letter as another button, it* doesn't get a key equivalent.  (Unless it's default or Cancel,* in which case it gets Return or Apple-period/Esc as usual.)** AlertWindow with the disk-swap icon always calls SysBeep2($C030).** 15-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** For a *default* Cancel button, Return and Esc and Apple-period* all work for the key equivalent.** 26-Mar-91 	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow flag bit 7 ($0080) makes it call ReleaseResource(3)* instead of ReleaseResource(-1), so if you locked your resource* it will stay in memory.** Leading blanks are now tolerated when computing AlertWindow key* equivalents.** 27-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow window positions are now forced to be at even X* positions (so that icon dithering comes out right in 640 mode).** 1-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow masks off System Window bit from TaskMaster so that* clicking in a System window beeps.  Also getting a wInDrag beeps* (this can happen if you used WindowGlobal to leave a window* hilited!).** 2-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Oops, PollForInsertions wasn't conditioning the carry flag after* calling ScanDevices.** 7-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow bit $0100 forces a disk-insert scan even if there's no* disk-swap icon.** 8-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Dang, the 7-Apr addition made it usually display no icon.  Fixed.** 12..13-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Adding new call HandleDiskInsert.** 14-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Tweaks to HandleDiskInsert (cursor handling).** 18-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Made DoModalWindow zero out the MWGetCtlPart value so that we return* part code zero if no TrackControl was performed (for example, when* a keypress activates a control with a key equivalent).** After attempting to eject a disk, I now record its *current* status* rather than always recording it offline if the DControl Eject gave* me no error.** 21-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** More work on the HandleDiskInsert rename dialog.** Make DoModalWindow update the thing before allowing SysBeep2* to trigger.** 23-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Add flag bit to HandleDiskInsert to simulate a duplicate-disk* error, for use by the Finder.** Fix the above DoModalWindow fix to not be bothered by another* window's deactivate event.** 30-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** When DoModalWindow calls MWSetMenuProc to get the menu proc, it was* passing NIL; now it passes $FFFFFFFF.** 8-May-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed major AlertWindow problem where having the separator character* in a substitution string would fry.  Now I compile the text once,* search for a character that does not appear anywhere, and use that* for the separator character.** 9-May-91	Dave Lyons** Increased HandleDiskInsert Volume pCount to 8 so Volume will return* fileSysID/etc even if a dup-vol error comes back.  So now the right* number of characters are allowed in the rename-disk edit line.** 20-May-91	Dave Lyons** DoModalWindow--new flag bit mwWantActivate must be set for DoModalWindow* to return activate/deactivate events.  Otherwise it just eats them for* speed.  On activate/deactivate, no longer redraws $87FFxxxx controls.** In HandleDiskInsert SetDevStatus, we don't do anything unless* fDoDeviceScan or fUpdateDevStatus is set in the flags.** HandleDiskInsert RenameVolume gives the user another chance to rename* the thing if an error occurs.** 21-May-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert:  Dim the Rename button when there's no new name* entered.** 10-Jun-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert now calls InitCursor when you hit the Rename* button.** FindCursorCtl now ignores invisible controls.** 27-Jun-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed AlertWindow to beep if you click in a window's info bar,* grow box, zoom box, or close box.** 8-Jul-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert calls SysBeep2($4033 = sbBadDisk + sbDefer) when* it detects an I/O error or an unrecognized file system.** 5-Aug-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow bit $0200 means there is are four bytes of custom icon* data, which are an rIcon resource ID.  The icon must be available* in memory, or online--it must not cause another AlertWindow to pop* up because the OS wants a disk!** 16-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow disk-swap icon no longer calls LoadResource at AlertWindow* time; instead, we load it at WindStartUp.  This way we do not try a* reentrant call to LoadResource if LoadResource causes the OS to prompt* for a disk!** Added missing LDX #$FFFF on releasing rAlertString resource if bit* $0080 is clear.  Was not releasing resources reliably.** 4-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert--tabbing to a new control returns the handle and id* of the new control, not the old one.** AlertWindow--sets Font Flags to $0004 so you can have 16-color text* in 640-mode if you want.** 10-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert special-cases error $0021 (bad control code) from* a Format to a 3.5 drive, to put up the special ErrorWindow(99)* explaining that the user tried to format 800K as 1400K or vice versa.** HandleDiskInsert ignores Apple tape drives unless fCheckTapeDrives* is set (flags $0200).** ErrorWindow always uses cool button positions.** 24-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert has logic to check for never-writeable devices* and read-only file systems, when handling a duplicate-name volume.* There are two new dialogs (rAlertString $07FF0E01 and $07FF0E02 in* Sys.Resources) for these cases.** 27-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert special-cases AppleShare (can never rename an* AppleShare volume).** DoModalWindow invalidates static text control on activates *if** the control's fTextCanDim bit is set.** 30-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** The can't-rename dialogs now force an arrow cursor (was already* being restored).** AlertWindow calls WindowGlobal($FFFE) right after creating the* window, instead of when the window gets closed.  This way we don't* lose the activate event for window behind the alert.** 5-Nov-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow now unlocks the rAlertString resource handle before* releasing it (for dispose, doesn't matter; for the alertNoDispose* bit, this leaves the handle unlocked!).** AlertWindow disables key translation during the call, unless there* are buttons with high-ASCII equivalents.** 13-Nov-91	Dave Lyons** FindCursorCtl--removed special casing for TE controls.** 14-Nov-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert--for error $5A, put up a disk-damaged dialog and* let them eject/initialize (was ignoring error $5A).** 21-Nov-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert polling was doing DInfo pcount=8, which caused* device access.  Now uses pcount=3 (like it did a couple months* ago) when just checking status.** 320-mode rename dialog now works (has separate window/ctl templates).** 22-Nov-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert rename dialog must draw icon manually instead of* using an icon button control, since the defproc cannot be guaranteed* to be loaded.** HandlediskInsert rename AlertWindow calls now set the fAlertNoDispose* bit.** AlertWindow no longer unlocks rAlertString resources that are marked* locked in their resource attributes.** 2-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert calls GetFileInfo after a successful Volume call,* because the HFS FST can detect a damaged disk during GetFileInfo.** 3-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow is using a lot of stack space, largely thanks to TaskMaster* and DrawControls.  When GS/OS calls us, the stack is near $BFFF; there* are 2 pages or less of stack available, so we're hosing GS/OS direct page* when it overruns.** The fix:  after our direct page stuff set up, we switch to a new 6-page* stack segment (size = ExtraStackSize).  If we can't allocate a separate* stack, we don't call ScanDevices.** On closing alert, AlertWindow now flushes keyDown events only if it* was scanning for disk insertions.** 5-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** When HandleDiskInsert renames a disk, it sets the TrustMe bit in the* new 3rd parameter, so that the OS does not do RenamePathname, rename* VCRs/FCRs, or change its record of the boot volume name.** 6-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow now uses correct key equivalents for Cancel button even* when it is padded with leading blanks, or when Cancel is capitalized* in a nonstandard way.** 9-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert:  Add new flag bit, hdiUnreadable ($0100), that* makes me skip the Volume call and assume the device is unreadable* (that Volume would return error $27).** 10-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert NewWindow2 for the rename-this-disk window is* now by Pointer instead of Resource, so that NewWindow2 does not* detach my handy pre-loaded resource!** After HandleDiskInsert calls ErrorWindow, it calls LoadResource* to re-lock the rErrorString $07FF0096 and -7 handles, so they* can't get purged.** 17-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** AlertWindow now sets system preferences to prompt for disk,* no Cancel button.  (Caller is typically not checking for an* error, and it's dangerous to let them act on the result-space* garbage as a user choice.)** Added alertFullColorBit ($0400); AlertWindow only does the* SetFontFlags(4) if this bit is set, for compatibility.** 8-Jan-92	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert now does a SendRequest(systemSaysEjecting) when* it ejects a disk.  This way EasyMount can avoid doing a bogus open* on a duplicate volume that was mounted and then ejected.** 16-Jan-92	Dave Lyons** Optimizations in AlertWindow:  Killed 10 bytes of dead storage,* and a dozen or two bytes of redundant code (noted by Yvan Koenig).* Made the AlertWindow "Cancel" check more easily localizable (cost* ten bytes).** 17-Jan-92	Dave Lyons** Make AlertWindow SetKeyTranslation calls *not* affect Battery RAM* (key translation was getting permanently turned off if you rebooted* during an AlertWindow, like the "Restart" dialog).** 31-Jan-92	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert never handles an Apple Tape Drive (it just returns* no error, without making a Volume call).** HandleDiskInsert now treats a still-online disk as an insert if* there is a disk-switched condition returned from DStatus.************************************************************************* BEGIN 6.0.1** 6-Mar-92	Dave Lyons** Added new UpdateWindow call.** 19-Jun-92	Dave Lyons** Added flags word parameter to UpdateWindow.  DoModalWindow and* AlertWindow updated to pass flags.  DoModalWindow sets bit 31 of* the default wContDraw.** AlertWindow now uses UpdateWindow to update other people'sl windows,* if those windows are smart enough (wContDraw bit 31 set).** 10-Jul-92	Dave Lyons** Bits 31-24 of the updateProc to HandleDiskInsert are now honored* even if the rest of the pointer is NIL.  This way you can flag your* window as not needing GS/OS for its update. -- Also, we never* replace a window's existing wContDraw procedure, if it has one* (we give it a wContDraw on the first call if it doesn't have one).** 28-Oct-92	Dave Lyons** HandleDiskInsert now treats error $51 (directory damaged) like error* $5A (damaged bitmap).  Puts up "This disk is damaged and can't be* used.  Eject/Initialize".** 30-Nov-92	Dave Lyons** Added "jsr setValues" after LECut, LEPaste, TECut, TEPaste, so that* DoModalWindow returns the control IDs when the user changes the* an editable control's contents by cutting or pasting.** 19-Feb-93	Dave Lyons** Changed the HandleDiskInsert duplicate-disk dialog to use a Note* icon instead of a 3.5" disk icon (since it happens for many kinds* of disks that look nothing like the icon).** 21-Mar-93	Dave Lyons** DoModalWindow handles an Update event with mwUpdateAll clear by* calling UpdateWindow with flags of $0000 for the dialog window,* but $8000 for other windows--so the other windows update only if* it's safe for them to background-update.  If the mwUpdateAll bit* is set, it always passes flags of $0000.** Cleaned out a bunch of crusty comments & dead code from AlertWindow.** 23-Mar-93	Dave Lyons** Changed UpdateWindow to return an error for a background update* of a System window, since System windows should alwyas get updated* from inside SystemEvent.  (Some people, like ModalDialog, are calling* GetNextEvent and ingoring the return flag that says "you should not* handle this, it's already taken care of by SystemEvent".)** Changed DoModalWindow so it doesn't invalidate controls on an* activate if the window's fCtlTie bit is set, saying that the control* states are independent of the window state.** 5-Apr-93	Dave Lyons (for 6.0.1d17)** On a DoModalWindow background update, zero out code so we will blink* insertion points even if we never handling pending updates behind our* dialog.***********************************************************************	Blanks off	String asis	print push	print off	INCLUDE 'ALL.MACROS'	INCLUDE 'e16.control'	include 'e16.event'		;22-Jan-91 DAL	include 'e16.lineedit'	;22-Jan-91 DAL	include 'e16.locator'	;8-Jan-92 DAL	include 'WindMgrEquates.asm'	print pop;===========================================;          Create an Alert Window.;===========================================;;   IN:    PUSH:WORD - space for result, button number selected.;          PUSH:WORD - bit 0 = 0 if substitution strings are C type (null or return).;	   bit 0 = 1 if substitution strings are Pascal type (length byte).;	   bit 1&2 = 00 if alert string passed is a pointer.;	   bit 1&2 = 01 if alert string passed is a handle.;	   bit 1&2 = 11 if alert string passed is a resource ID.;	   bit 3 = don't adjust text rectangle for icon;	   bit 4 = do a SysBeep2 call;	   bit 5 = space buttons unevenly;	   bit 6 = skip initial disk-insert scan;	   bit 7 = don't dipose of resource (make it purgeable instead);	   bit 8 = scan for disk insertions even without disk-swap icon;                      bit 9 = custom icon is resource;                      bit 10 = full color--set FontFlags to $0004;          PUSH:LONG - pointer to substitution strings.;          PUSH:LONG - pointer to alert	string.;;  OUT:    WORD - button number selected.;;===========================================	EXPORT AlertWindowAlertWindow	PROC	import FlushKeyEvents,WindowUpdateCountExtraStackSize	equ $0600	;added 3-Dec-91 DALalertResourceID	equ 1	;ID of loaded alert string resource, NIL if none.alertStrgHand	equ alertResourceID+4windRect	equ alertStrgHand+4	;RECT of window's content.xxLocInfo	equ windRect+8	;SCB.xxImage	equ xxLocInfo+2	;Pointer to pixel image.xxWidth	equ xxImage+4	;Width of image.xxBounds	equ xxWidth+2	;Bounds RECT of image.terminate	equ xxBounds+8separator	equ terminate+2butt1	equ separator+2butt2	equ butt1+4butt3	equ butt2+4handle	equ butt3+4ptr	equ handle+4ptr2	equ ptr+4taskRec	equ ptr2+4	;Task record overlaps work.TheWork	equ taskRec+exTaskRecSizeDoingButtons	equ TheWork+8	;added 25-Nov-90 DALdiskInsertFlag	equ DoingButtons+2	;added 7-Mar-91 DALtheNewSeparator	equ diskInsertFlag+2 ;added 8-May-91 DALoldKeyTranslation	equ theNewSeparator+2 ;added 5-Nov-91 DALoldStack	equ oldKeyTranslation+2 ;added 3-Dec-91 DALoldSysPrefs	equ oldStack+2	;added 17-Dec-91 DALrealDrawIconFlag	equ oldSysPrefs+2alertWind	equ realDrawIconFlag+2saveDpage	equ alertWind+4saveDbank	equ saveDpage+2returnAddr	equ saveDbank+1alertStrg	equ returnAddr+6substrgs	equ alertStrg+4strgType	equ substrgs+4result	equ strgType+2strgTypeBit	equ 1alertStrgBit	equ 6	;bits 1-2alertStrgPtr	equ 0	;value for bits 1-2alertStrgHandle	equ 2	;value for bits 1-2alertStrgResource	equ 4	;value for bits 1-2alertRectBit	equ $08	;14-Nov-90 DAL: bit 3 = don't subtract icon width from rectalertSoundBit	equ $10	;9-Mar-91 DAL: bit 4 = call SysBeep2alertSpacingBit	equ $20	;13-Mar-91 DAL: bit 5 = space buttons unevenlyalertSkipScanBit	equ $40	;15-Mar-91 DAL: bit 6 = skip initial disk scanalertNoDisposeBit	equ $80	;26-Mar-91 DAL: bit 7 = don't dispose resourcealertDiskScanBit	equ $100	;7-Apr-91 DAL: bit 8 = default button on d